 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 535600,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Define and describe community ecology. Give an example.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1048696,
     "content_html": "It is the study of the number of individuals of one species in an area as well as how and why the number changes over time. An example would be counting the number of individuals of the Karner blue butterfly, a federally endangered species whose population density is highly influenced by the abundance of wild lupine."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048697,
     "content_html": "It is the study of the processes and consequences of interactions within and among different species within an area. An example would be the work of scientists who work in a marsh studying the various interactions of several populations of birds, crabs, and grasses without studying the water or air quality."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048698,
     "content_html": "It is the study of the physiological, morphological, and behavioral adaptations that enable individuals to live in specific habitats. An example would be the work of scientists who work in a marsh studying the various interactions of several populations of birds, crabs, and grasses without studying the water or air quality."
    },
    {
     "id": 1048699,
     "content_html": "It is the study of the processes and consequences of interactions within and among different species within an area. An example would be counting the number of individuals of the Karner blue butterfly, a federally endangered species whose population density is highly influenced by the abundance of wild lupine."
    }
